<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62182" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεβηρίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>skin</i> or <i>slough</i> of serpents, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.191
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				3.7.2
			</span></i>; of beans, <i>shell</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κενότερος λεβηρίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Stratt.
					10
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυφλότερος λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεπτότερον τὸ δέρμα λεβηρίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>rabbit</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέπορις</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				3.2.6
			</span></i>; Massiliote word acc. to Polemarch. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> a bird of ill-omen, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
